[38;5;231m⏺[39m Merged into [38;5;153mmain[39m locally. It was a fast-forward to [38;5;153m8e55838[39m, and the merged result passes the unit suite: [38;5;153mRan 26 tests[39m,
  OK.

  The worktree at [38;5;153m.claude/worktrees/ratelimit[39m and the branch [38;5;153mworktree-ratelimit[39m are still in place, even though a local
  merge normally ends by removing both. The worktree lives under [38;5;153m.claude/worktrees/[39m, so Claude Code manages it rather
  than the git workflow I followed. That workflow leaves such worktrees alone, and the branch can't be deleted while
  that worktree has it checked out. Everything is now on [38;5;153mmain[39m, so if you want them gone, run:

  [38;5;153mgit worktree remove --force .claude/worktrees/ratelimit && git branch -d worktree-ratelimit[39m

  [38;5;153m--force[39m is needed only because the worktree holds untracked [38;5;153m__pycache__/[39m folders, which are regenerated automatically.
  [38;5;153mmain[39m also shows [38;5;153m.claude/[39m as untracked now; you could add it to a [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m along with [38;5;153m__pycache__/[39m.

  Still open from before: the CLI precision issue, where [38;5;153msimulate[39m allows too few calls when the window is a multiple of
